<div class="<%= layout_framework_classes %>">
  <div class="<%= layout_framework_title_classes %>">
    <%= render 'framework/page_header', page_name: :v3_upgrade_guide %>
  </div>

  <div class="<%= layout_framework_content_classes %>">
    <%= render_framework_intro_paragraph(:v3_upgrade_guide) %>

    <div class="space-y-16">
      <section class="space-y-6">
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'From Framework 3.0 or 3.1') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            Upgrade and rerender: your plugin looks the same until you opt into 3.2 and 3.3 features. Two things are worth reviewing.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 <%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            <li><strong>Numbered border levels are deprecated:</strong> <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">border--h-1</code> through <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">border--h-7</code> (and vertical counterparts) still render, but will be removed in Framework 4.0. Prefer the shade-step rail (<code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">border--h-10</code> to <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">border--h-75</code>) in new markup. See <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :border) %>.</li>
            <li><strong>Themed screens ignore dark mode:</strong> if you add a <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">screen--theme-&lt;id&gt;</code> class, <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">screen--dark-mode</code> no longer applies. A theme is a complete color statement. See <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :themes) %>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-6">
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'From Framework v2') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            v3 is structurally backward compatible with v2: your class names still compile and render. One visual change needs review: v3 rebuilt the <code class="<%= framework_section_code_classes %>">1bit</code> grayscale dither patterns on a 14-step linear scale, so most shade names produce different lightness values than they did in v2.
          </p>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            The full shade-by-shade migration table lives in the
            <%= link_to 'Framework 3.1 upgrade guide', framework_page_path('v3_upgrade_guide', version: '3.1'), class: 'font-medium hover:underline' %>.
            It lists each shade's v2 and v3 lightness and which v3 shade restores the original look.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-6">
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Verifying the Upgrade') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            Use the Raw / Preview toggle in Device Preview to compare full-bright token values against panel-accurate output. To check theme behavior, pick a Style in the screen picker and confirm your plugin stays legible under each theme.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-6">
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <%= framework_heading(3, 'Next Steps') %>
          <p class="<%= framework_section_description_classes %>">
            Head to the <%= render DocsRef.new(page: :v3_enhancement_guide) %> to make your plugin theme-ready and to adopt adaptive charts and icons.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <%= render 'framework/page_navigation' %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
